r to  toxicity where the anger isn't it's when  the anger isn't rooted in oh I don't get  to have the thing I like but instead  becomes why do they get a nice thing I  hate them for that and that honestly I  think that is the line for toxic fandom  is the point at which it crosses over  from well first of all hate is a strong  emotion it's a stronger word and it's  when I try to not use and not because  I'm like afraid of the word hate but  like it's supposed to be a potent thing  and I think people overuse it and if  they truly are feeling that level of  hate with things that you know as much  as some people claim to be that that  concerns me on a different level but you  know like I don't think it's toxic to  say I hate what has happened to Star  Wars under Kathleen Kennedy's watch I do  think it starts at toxic to say I hate  Kathleen Kennedy when you start  directing your anger away from the  abstract away from the individual pieces  of art the way from away from the  franchise and at people when you start  targeting your anger at people be it  the creators be it critics  who don't agree with your assessment of  a piece of art be it fans who are happy  with something that you're unhappy with  when you start directing your anger at  individuals real people buy and true  nouveau in I mean I can get angry I can  get angry and ranty but I tried very  very hard to direct that at the work and  not the people and even when I express  my frustration at the people I try and  really have it be over this specific  narrative thing that they did and not go  down the path of you're a terrible  person I hate you because I don't want  to hate somebody for making a piece of  art I didn't like and I think there's  also a tendency to really over demonize  certain fundamental political views that  we don't agree with and that kind of all  gets rolled into this as well so and  again I think ultimately that should be  coming down to execution rather than  concept so when people who have not even  seen something like Shira are denouncing  it because they believe it feeds into a  left-leaning political philosophy and  they're condemning it for that without  even considering how those ideas are  expressed the qualities of the piece of  art that has those concepts behind it  that's wealth at best that's frustrating  so like for me I love the movie 300 I  think it's a fantastic movie I  fundamentally disagree with a lot of the  philosophical underpinnings of that  movie and I certainly do not agree with  the major philosophies of the hero  characters but it's still a great movie  visually astonishing it's really  phenomenally paced it's well acted it's  engaging as heck the characters are  charismatic it's a great movie that has  underpinnings that I don't agree with  but again it's not what it's about it's  how it is about it and I would and if I  didn't like 300 I would I like to think  at least I would not like it because it  wasn't a well-made film not because it  espoused philosophical ideas that I  disagree with we've drawn so many hard  lines lately where I'm on this side  you're on that side and anything I see  over there on that side of this line  that's the worst and there is no good  that can come from anything on that side  it's kind of the approach that people  tend to take but here's where I want to  end on a slightly nah hopefuls not the  right word reassuring note for all that  I'm saying and all that I deal with I do  still believe very firmly and every  thing that I see every time I actually  stop and think and look and analyze  carefully backs this up these elements  that I'm talking about these fans that  exhibit toxic behaviors they are very  loud they are very good at driving the  conversation they're also the minority  they disproportionately take up an  irritatingly large amount of the  conversation because of how loud they  are they become very difficult to ignore  but they are not the majority I feel  incredibly confident in saying that  because every time I have actually like  really basically run the numbers and and  it's it's easy to lose sight especially  in social media because I think it's a  very human thing where you know you put  something out there be it a tweet a  video what have you a hundred people say  they really like it one person says it's  craft you put more weight in  that because I think a lot of us is and  unless you have like a bulletproof ego a  lot of us assume there's more honesty  and criticism than compliment but if you  actually run the numbers more often than  not or and I can't say this is the  experience for everybody but this is my  experience when I look at the numbers  when I compare how many really horrible  comments I have to delete off something  like Star Wars video or or you know when  I talk about lgbtq+ representation or  things of that nature as much as I hate  having to do that and it pains me every  single time I have to delete a comment  or block somebody off the channel I also  can reassure myself this is not most  people and it's easy to lose sight of  that because most people don't make  waves  most people have more measured feelings  and unfortunately it's oftentimes hard  to hear the voice going well you know  there's good and there's bad to be had  here in the middle of a shouting match  between the extremes the middle ground  gets drowned out even though the middle  ground is the majority I I do very  sincerely believe that when it comes to  most of these things and I think that's  the thing that we really need to try and  keep sight of the Toxic fan elements  well first of all the other thing I'll  add they're not new they haven't been  created by the internet by reddit by  fortune by whatever these have simply  given them a platform for them to come  together as a more unified force but I  can think back to my own childhood I  think in grade school of of slightly  older you know maybe by only four or  five years but slightly older Star Wars  fans giving massive grief to  younger Star Wars fans because those  younger Star Wars fans liked the Ewok  cartoon i I don't think this has been  created by the technology we have the  technology we have simply allows these  people to have a megaphone but again we  have to remind ourselves that these  people are new we've been dealing with  them forever and just because they're  shouting louder does not mean that we  have to give them the attention that  they want I'm not gonna go so far as to  claim if we ignore them they'll go away  no they won't  they never will but we can you know what  we actually can do we can address their  argue their arguments their toxicity  even without engaging them directly we  can agree amongst each other yeah that  thing that happened over there when this  group of people drove an actor from a  film off of social media through a  concentrated harassment and threat  campaign yeah that was awful wasn't it  we don't actually need to engage them  and go you're terrible for doing that  because engaging them is what they want  we don't have to we can talk about it we  can talk about what's going on and we  can go yeah we're not gonna be that we  don't actually have to engage and I  think I will wrap up on that note so the  very loaded topic of toxic fandoms what  are your thoughts on this I know there's  a bit of a divisive topic be respectful  and I like I said I tried very hard to  not name names so please don't let the  comment section devolve into a list of  who you think the worst offenders are I  I don't care let's talk about the  element we don't have to name names we  can still have the conversation  regardless but whatever your thoughts  are drop something down in the comments  let's talk about it whole bunch of stuff  you can do because there's buttons and  there's links including a link to my  patreon if you feel like lending me your  support in that fashion if you don't  don't worry about  otherwise you can check out too if you  don't want to look at those don't have  to worry about that either because at  the end of the day folks you are the  council I just run the meetings and  until next time this council is a jerk  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

